7592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344994 #edb/ref 1071 "Find  ${lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344994 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "267b24cc-56d4-5780-90e2-1ea13cc5ba4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344994 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz}=\\frac{1\\cdot {2}^{2}-1\\cdot {2}^{2}}{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{(x-y){z}^{2}}{(y-x)z} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}-\\frac{(x-y){z}^{2}}{(x-y)z} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}(-z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,1,2)}(-z) & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186377699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "117ca5de-bfde-5504-8e9b-162dc1ee9296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/r