b/ref 1072 #uuid "113d22b7-0222-5499-8d44-de1af29900a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407846 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{3}-xy}{{x}^{3}y} & =\\frac{{0}^{3}-2(0)}{{2}^{3}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{3}-xy}{{x}^{3}y} & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{y({y}^{2}-x)}{{x}^{3}y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{y}({y}^{2}-x)}{{x}^{3}\\cancel{y}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{{x}^{3}} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}-2}{{2}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-\\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23171e8d-210d-5c2c-9bfd-bb23fda5150e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186377708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61b825c0-1272-5e4c-b3ff-4f0f75ec0886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "80843e02-eff6-534a-9c80-13ab1c07a9fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407847 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
